      "content": "Identifying erythema and inflammation in darker skin tones requires recognizing that the normal skin pigmentation can mask or alter the appearance of redness. Instead of bright redness, inflammation may manifest as hyperpigmentation, lightening, or a subtle change in skin texture. Dermatologists often rely on palpation, assessing induration (firmness), and observing satellite lesions in addition to visual inspection when evaluating darker skin.",
